5 Commands
**********

This chapter documents all interactive commands provided by whisper-dvr.

 -- Command: whisper-dvr
     List audio files from the configured DVR directory and transcribe
     the selected file using whisper.el.  The transcription is inserted
     at point in the current buffer.

     This command performs the following checks before proceeding:

        • Verifies that the current buffer is not read-only.

        • Warns if the current buffer is not visiting a file (prompts
          for confirmation to continue).

        • Verifies that the DVR directory exists and contains audio
          files.

     The completion interface displays each file with its name,
     human-readable size, and modification timestamp.

     Keybinding suggestion:

          (global-set-key (kbd "C-c w d") 'whisper-dvr)

 -- Command: whisper-dvr-set-directory dir
     Interactively set the DVR directory to DIR.  When called
     interactively, prompts for the directory path with completion.

     This is useful when you have multiple recording devices or when the
     mount point changes between sessions.

          ;; Called programmatically:
          (whisper-dvr-set-directory "/path/to/new/dvr")


