7 Testing
*********

Whisper-dvr includes a comprehensive test suite using ERT (Emacs Lisp
Regression Testing).  This chapter describes how to run the tests and
the structure of the test suite.

7.1 Running Tests
=================

7.1.1 From the Command Line
---------------------------

Use the provided Makefile to run all tests:

     cd /path/to/whisper-dvr
     make test

   To run tests with verbose output:

     make test-verbose

7.1.2 From Within Emacs
-----------------------

Load the test file and run ERT:

     (load-file "whisper-dvr-test.el")
     M-x ert RET t RET

   To run a specific test:

     M-x ert RET whisper-dvr-test-default-directory RET

7.2 Test Categories
===================

The test suite is organized into several categories:

*Unit Tests: Custom Variables*
     Tests that verify the default values of customization options.

*Unit Tests: whisper-dvr-list-audio-files*
     Tests for the file listing function, including error handling for
     non-existent directories and extension filtering.

*Unit Tests: whisper-dvr-format-file-entry*
     Tests for the file entry formatting function, verifying correct
     display of filenames, sizes, and timestamps.

*Unit Tests: whisper-dvr-set-directory*
     Tests for the directory setting command.

*Unit Tests: whisper-dvr*
     Tests for the main interactive command, including buffer state
     checks.

*Integration Tests*
     End-to-end tests that verify the complete workflow from file
     selection to transcription invocation.

*Edge Case Tests*
     Tests for unusual inputs such as special characters in filenames,
     very large files, and zero-size files.

7.3 Test Helpers
================

The test file provides several helper functions and variables for
mocking:

 -- Variable: whisper-dvr-test--mock-files
     Mock file list for testing.

 -- Variable: whisper-dvr-test--mock-attrs
     Mock file attributes for testing.

 -- Variable: whisper-dvr-test--whisper-file-called
     Boolean flag tracking whether ‘whisper-file’ was called.

 -- Variable: whisper-dvr-test--whisper-file-arg
     Stores the argument passed to ‘whisper-file’.

 -- Function: whisper-dvr-test--reset-state
     Reset all test state variables to their initial values.

 -- Function: whisper-dvr-test--make-mock-attrs size mtime
     Create mock file attributes with the given SIZE (in bytes) and
     MTIME (modification time).


